 "notes": "Umm Gamar reef with its crescent islet, the moorings on the south plateau (14-24 m) with the three small glassfish ergs on its eastern corner, the usual dive east to the drop-off and north along the wall to the three chimney pinnacles and back on the current, caves in the east and west walls and the coral garden at the northern tip. Reef, islet, light and mooring come from OpenStreetMap; the features and route from dive-centre site descriptions (divers-guide.com, redseacreatures.com), placed by description, so the plateau extent and the erg and pinnacle positions are approximate. Reef data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).",
